{title: O Praise Him (All This for a King)}
{artist: David Crowder}
{key: A#}
{capo: 3}

{comment: Verse 1}
[A#]Turn your ear to heaven and [A#/A]hear the noise inside  [D#2]
The [A#]sound of angels' awe, the sound of angels[A#/A]' songs
[D#2]All this for a king, we could [Cm7]join and sing, all to Christ the King    [D#2]

{comment: Pre-Chorus 1}
[F]How constant, how divine, [D#2]this song of [F]ours will rise    [D#2]
[F]How constant, how divine, [D#2]this song of [F]ours will rise, will rise [D#2]

{comment: Chorus 1}
[A#]O Praise Him, O praise [F/A]Him, He is Holy, He [Gm7]is Holy  [D#2]    [Cm7]
[A#]O Praise Him, O praise [F/A]Him, He is Holy, He [Gm7]is Holy  [D#2]    [Cm7]

{comment: Verse 2}
[A#]Turn your gaze to heaven [A#/A]and raise a joyous noise  [D#2]
The [A#]sound of salvation come, the sound of rescued [A#/A]ones
[D#2]All this for a king, angels join [Cm]to sing, all for Christ our King  [D#2]

{comment: Pre-Chorus 2}
[F]How infinite and sweet, [D#2]this love [F]so rescuing    [D#2]
[F]O, how infinitely sweet, [D#2]this [F]great love that has redeemed    [D#2]

{comment: Chorus 2}
[A#]Allelulia, [F/A]Allelulia, He [Gm7]is Holy, He [D#2]is [Cm7]Holy
